---

Quanta is a sovereign peer-to-peer web and value network: no server, no cloud,
no intermediary. The native coin is QUANTA (smallest unit: µQTA, 1 QUANTA =
1,000,000 µQTA).

This software bundles, links against, or otherwise depends on third-party
open-source components, each distributed under its own license. Notable
dependencies include (non-exhaustive):

  - Iroh / iroh-gossip / iroh-blobs (QUIC P2P transport)        — MIT / Apache-2.0
  - ed25519-dalek (Ed25519 signatures)                          — BSD-3-Clause
  - aes-gcm (AES-256-GCM authenticated encryption)              — Apache-2.0 / MIT
  - argon2 (Argon2id key derivation)                            — Apache-2.0 / MIT
  - blake3 (BLAKE3 hashing)                                     — Apache-2.0 / CC0-1.0
  - zeroize (secret zeroization)                                — Apache-2.0 / MIT
  - libsql (embedded SQL storage)                              — MIT
  - crdts (PN-Counter CRDTs)                                    — Apache-2.0 / MIT
  - Tauri (desktop runtime)                                     — Apache-2.0 / MIT
  - Svelte / SvelteKit (frontend)                              — MIT

Refer to each dependency's source distribution for the authoritative license
terms.
